{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 4.5% a year from $70.3 billion in FY2016 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F205], but the path was a step change, not a straight line."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue jumped 19.8% in FY2020 to $93.6 billion [F5][D183] and another 13.3% in FY2021 to $106.0 billion [F6][D230], then fell in each of the last three years to $104.8 billion [F10][D416]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 surge came from a 19.3% comparable sales increase [P51], and FY2025's decline reflected comparable sales down 2.6% on a 2.2% traffic drop [P14]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating income compounded at just 0.6% over the window [F207], and net income fell 9.4% in FY2025 to $3.71 billion [F44][D418]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Merchandise sales were 98.0% of revenue in FY2025 [D465] and fell 2.0%, a 2.0pp drag on total growth [D466][D467]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Food & beverage grew 1.3% in FY2025 and contributed 0.3pp [D507][D508], while apparel fell 4.7% for a 0.7pp drag [D564][D565] and household essentials fell 3.2% for 0.6pp [D514][D515]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Food & beverage's share of revenue rose from 19.6% in FY2017 to 23.0% in FY2025 [D484][D506], the clearest mix shift toward frequency categories."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income fell 8.1% in FY2025 against a 1.7% revenue decline [D417][D416], so there was no operating leverage; SG&A fell 2.0% [D432] while cost of revenue fell 1.3% [D431]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS fell 8.2% in FY2025 [D420] against net income down 9.4% [D418], as the diluted share count fell 1.3% [D434]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin was 4.9% in FY2025 [F34], below the 5.6% window median [D590] and far from the 8.4% FY2021 high [D589], though above the 3.5% FY2022 low [D588]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2025 margin fell 0.3pp [D429], with cost of revenue a 0.3pp drag [D440] as the gross margin rate slipped to 27.9% from 28.2% [P12]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "SG&A was 20.6% of revenue, flat on FY2024, including a 0.6pp benefit from interchange fee settlements offset by 0.2pp of business transformation costs [P11]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The largest move was FY2022, when operating margin fell 4.9pp [D290] as cost of revenue was a 4.6pp drag [D301], driven by markdowns, excess inventory and supply-chain costs [P38]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net margin of 3.5% [F54] sits close to operating margin of 4.9% [F34], with the 22.3% effective tax rate [D403] and $445 million interest expense [X66] the main below-the-line items."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow was $6.56 billion and free cash flow $2.84 billion in FY2025 [F84][F104], a 2.7% free-cash-flow margin [D401] below the 4.5% window median [D596]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow fell from $7.37 billion in FY2024 [F83] on lower net earnings and lower accounts payable leverage [P7]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow covered net income 0.77 times in FY2025 [D405] against a 1.01 times window median [D599], and capex of $3.73 billion was 1.19 times D&A [F94][D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Capex rose 28.9% in FY2025 [D423] on increased investment in new stores and remodels [P5], and management guides to about $5 billion in FY2026 [P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash and investments were $10.1 billion against total debt of $14.4 billion in FY2025 [D408][D409], a net debt position of $4.30 billion [D410]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net debt was 4.1% of revenue [D411], better than the retail peer median of -3.5% [D613] and at the 50th percentile of six peers [D612]; the current ratio was 0.94x [F184]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Buybacks plus dividends were $2.46 billion in FY2025 [D412], 86.8% of free cash flow [D413], with $408 million of repurchases [X126] and $2.05 billion of dividends [X136]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The diluted share count fell from 582.5 million in FY2016 to 455.6 million in FY2025 [X107][X116], supporting EPS growth of 6.3% against net income growth of 3.4% [F210][F208]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue has declined three years running, from $109.1 billion in FY2022 to $104.8 billion in FY2025 [F7][F10][R1], with FY2025 comparable sales down 2.6% [P14]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The current ratio of 0.94x [F184][R2] is at the window median of 0.94x [D602], so the sub-1.0x reading reflects a normal working-capital-negative retail model rather than new stress."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The FY2022 burn coverage of 2.4 years [D276][R3] is stale, since free cash flow has been positive in every year since [F102][F103][F104]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Operating margin has fallen two years in a row, 0.4pp in total [F32][F33][F34][R4], and the FY2022 buyback figure was later restated to $2,646 million from $2,826 million [R5][X123]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Whether revenue stops falling: a FY2026 figure above $104.8 billion [F10] would reverse the three-year decline, while another drop confirms it."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the 5.6% window median [D590] or slips toward the 3.5% FY2022 low [D588], with the FY2026 10-K the place to check."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Whether capex lands near the guided $5 billion [P4], which against FY2025 free cash flow of $2.84 billion [F104] would pressure the 2.7% free-cash-flow margin [D401]."}
  ]}
]}
